+# Agent Note: Workspace selection failures reach the picker
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-17-workspace-selection-errors-reach-picker.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The Workspace picker closed as soon as a user selected an existing Workspace. `ConversationRoot` then called `selectWorkspace()` and caught a rejection only to remove the optimistic label. A protected directory, read-only profile, missing ledger, or other `session.create` / Workspace attachment failure therefore left the user on the unchanged screen with no explanation or retry action, even though the Host returned an actionable structured error. The sidebar add flow had the same terminal operation behind `WorkspaceRuntime.startSession()`, which logged failures to the console and resolved no outcome to its UI owner.
+
+## Decision
+
+Workspace selection is an asynchronous owner operation. `EmptyWorkspaceOwnerProps.onPick` returns `Promise<void>`, and `ConversationRoot` rolls back its optimistic label then rethrows the original rejection. `WorkspaceRuntime.startSession()` also returns a promise that settles after the target blank Session is selected and rejects unchanged when creation or attachment fails.
+
+`WorkspacePickFlow` owns presentation for both picker surfaces. Directory interaction and path-adoption failures continue to use the folder dialog and reopen the directory flow. A failure after a Workspace id exists uses a distinct **Couldn’t enter workspace** dialog, preserves the Host error message, and retries the same Workspace id without reopening directory selection. Workspace actions remain disabled while either directory adoption or Workspace selection is in flight.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Keep failures in runtime console diagnostics.** Rejected because remote and packaged clients do not expose that console as a user recovery surface, and the UI that initiated the operation already owns a retryable modal.
+
+**Convert operating-system failures into a small client-side error taxonomy.** Rejected because the Host owns filesystem policy and already reports the useful platform detail. Mapping only known POSIX or Windows codes would discard unanticipated provider and persistence failures.
+
+**Retry automatically.** Rejected because permission denial, protected system directories, and read-only storage are stable conditions. Automatic retries can create more partial blank Sessions and cannot tell the user what must change.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Selecting a Workspace no longer completes at the menu click; it completes when the corresponding blank Session is ready. Existing Workspace selection and post-adoption attachment share one retry path, while directory selection retains its separate retry semantics. The picker stores one operation-local retry closure while its modal is open; closing the modal drops it. No wire method, Host behavior, durable format, or filesystem policy changes.
+
+## Testing
+
+Workspace picker tests cover an `EPERM`-style selection rejection, visible Host text, retrying the same id, and successful modal dismissal. Conversation skeleton tests require owner rejection to remain observable while the optimistic label rolls back. Runtime and registration tests cover the promise-returning `startSession` call path. The focused GUI tests and affected-package typechecks pass.
